        <name>front</name>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns the object at the front/back of the list without removing it. The list must not be empty. Items are returned by const reference because changing their value could change their sort order. If you need to change the value of the front or back element then do so by a shift-modify-unshift or pop-modify-push sequence. Time complexity is O(1). </para>        </detaileddescription>
